    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0338" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg238"/>

                <head>No. 160.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence,
                    I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your note of the 2d instant, in
                    regard to the application of the Canadian Telegraph Company to land a cable in
                    Washington Territory, and to inform you that the matter is receiving the
                    consideration of this Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
